<% content_for :meta_title, "GitLocker FAQ" %>
<% content_for :meta_description,  "Check our Frequently Asked Questions" %>
<%= render BreadcrumbComponent.new(current_user, [{ text: "FAQ", url: faq_path }]) %>
<div id="" class="">
  <div class="mx-auto bg-gradient-to-l from-gray-200 via-fuchsia-200 to-stone-100 max-w-7xl px-6 py-24 sm:pt-32 lg:px-8 lg:py-40">
    <div class="lg:grid lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-8">
      <div class="lg:col-span-5">
        <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold  leading-10 tracking-tight text-gray-900">Frequently asked questions</h1>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7  text-gray-900">Can’t find the answer you’re looking for? Reach out to our support team at cody@gitlocker.com.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-10 lg:col-span-7 lg:mt-0">
        <dl class="space-y-10">
          <div>
            <dt class="text-base font-semibold leading-7  text-gray-900">How do I get started buying and selling code on the marketplace?</dt>
            <dd class="mt-2 text-base leading-7  text-gray-900">In order to buy and sell code on the marketplace all you need to do is make an account with GitLocker using your GitHub account. From there, in order to buy a product just browse through the marketplace to find a product you want and then when you find a product you like, click add to cart and then checkout. In order to sell, you need to click "add product" in the dropdown menu when you click on your user icon in the navigation bar. Follow the instructions on the "add product" page.</dd>
          </div>
<hr class="h-px my-8 bg-gray-200 border-0 dark:bg-gray-700">
          <div>
            <dt class="text-base font-semibold leading-7  text-gray-900">What kind of repositories can I sell?</dt>
            <dd class="mt-2 text-base leading-7  text-gray-900">You can sell any private GitHub repository that is currently in your GitHub account or any local repository on your computer.</dd>
          </div>
<hr class="h-px my-8 bg-gray-200 border-0 dark:bg-gray-700">
           <div>
            <dt class="text-base font-semibold  leading-7 text-gray-900">How much do I get to keep on my sales in the marketplace?</dt>
            <dd class="mt-2 text-base leading-7  text-gray-900">You get to keep 90% of your sales.</dd>
          </div>
<hr class="h-px my-8 bg-gray-200 border-0 dark:bg-gray-700">
           <div>
            <dt class="text-base font-semibold leading-7  text-gray-900">How many products can I list on the marketplace?</dt>
            <dd class="mt-2 text-base leading-7  text-gray-900">It depends what tier you are subscribed to. Our free tier allows for 10 products posted.</dd>
          </div>
<hr class="h-px my-8 bg-gray-200 border-0 dark:bg-gray-700">
           <div>
            <dt class="text-base font-semibold  leading-7 text-gray-900">How do I get paid in the marketplace?</dt>
            <dd class="mt-2 text-base leading-7  text-gray-900">Go to the "Get Paid" section in the dropdown menu when you click on your user icon in the navigation bar and click the button to withdraw via Stripe. There is a 7 day holding period giving the buyer a chance to ask for a refund.</dd>
          </div>
<hr class="h-px my-8 bg-gray-200 border-0 dark:bg-gray-700">
           <div>
            <dt class="text-base font-semibold  leading-7 text-gray-900">How do I create a private repository on GitHub?</dt>
            <dd class="mt-2 text-base leading-7  text-gray-900">Use this link to learn how to configure a private GitHub repository: <span class="font-bold underline"><%=link_to "Making a GitHub Repo", "https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/creating-and-managing-repositories/quickstart-for-repositories", :target => "_blank" %></span></dd>
          </div>
<hr class="h-px my-8 bg-gray-200 border-0 dark:bg-gray-700">
           <div>
            <dt class="text-base font-semibold  leading-7 text-gray-900">Where do I go to learn more about coding?</dt>
            <dd class="mt-2 text-base leading-7  text-gray-900">You can go to <span class="font-bold underline"><%=link_to "coding resources", resources_path %></span> to see all the different free and paid options for learning to code.</dd>
          </div>
<hr class="h-px my-8 bg-gray-200 border-0 dark:bg-gray-700">

          <!-- More questions... -->
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
